      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nClear HybridEP routing and dispatch metadata references after combine. Autograd retains the handles needed for backward.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nFixes #8409\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [x] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel, I have added or updated its bit-exact determinism test and registered it in tests/unit_tests/determinism/kernels/manifest.py\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [x] I have run the autoformatter.sh on my PR\n\nExtended the existing HybridEP routing-mode test to check cleanup and manager reuse. All four routing/fusion cases ran on eight GB200 GPUs.\n\nSeparate GPU checks verified exact outputs and gradients with delayed backward, and exact losses, gradients, and weights over ten full CUDA graph replays with static-capacity dispatch. See the linked issue for scope and results.\n\nNo functional test, kernel, type signature, API, or configuration change. The issue documents the finding. Please apply determinism-exempt for the reference cleanup. Optional mypy checks reported errors; no clean type-check result is claimed.\n\n### Code review\n\nOpen as a draft. Mark ready after CI passes and merge conflicts are resolved.\n",
